# # DriftSense — 05: Anomaly Detection Engine, Materiality & Severity (v2)
#
# **Runtime Type:** Python 3 (CPU or GPU)  
# **Estimated Runtime:** ~1-3 minutes  
# **RAM Needed:** ~2-4 GB  
# **Disk Needed:** ~1 GB  
# **Expected Outputs:**  
# - Detector Checkpoints: `runs/<run_id>/models/{conformal_interval,level_shift,rolling_threshold,zscore,iforest,ocsvm}.joblib`  
# - Validation Detections Matrix: `runs/<run_id>/val_detections_v2.csv`  
# - Validation Detection Metrics Report: `runs/<run_id>/val_detect_metrics_v2.json`  
# - Severity-Scored Incidents Table: `runs/<run_id>/val_severity_incidents.csv`  
# - Detection Visualizations: `runs/<run_id>/detection_comparison_v2.png`  
# - Cryptographically Verified Manifest: `runs/<run_id>/manifest.json`  
#
# > **CRITICAL EVALUATION & ISOLATION INVARIANTS (Rule C3, C6, C7):**  
# > - **Primary Detector:** Conformal prediction interval exceedance with temporal persistence ($k$-of-$n$) and business materiality filtering.  
# > - **Severity Tiers:** Actionable classification into Info, Low, Medium, and High tiers based on dollar impact, percentage jump, and persistence.  
# > - **A7.4 Test Quarantine:** The test partition ($D_{\text{test}}$) is strictly quarantined. Manifest records `holdout_touched=false`.

